Subject: [PATCH 1/4] schema: add migrations 0009-0016 for the yantrika.ai
 differentiator features

Foundation layer for twelve new features. Eight OPT-IN migrations, each
with the 0008-style banner and a rollback block:

  0009_demo_sandbox        ephemeral zero-signup demo sites, anon writes
                           scoped to exactly one DEMO-* site via an
                           x-yf-demo-token header resolved by yf_demo_site();
                           threat model documented in the file header
  0010_share_links         expiring read-only share tokens; the token grants
                           no table privileges at all and resolves only
                           through one kind-scoped SELECT-only RPC
  0011_replay              time-travel queries; adds incidents.closed_at plus
                           a stamping trigger (nothing previously recorded
                           when an incident stopped being open)
  0012_utilization         gap-capped utilization/cost rollups; the cost
                           assumption is operator-supplied, no currency or
                           rate is hardcoded
  0013_maintenance_explain structured `factors` on findings + a technician
                           feedback table feeding a by_factor accuracy view
  0014_inbound_ops         WhatsApp ack/assign/approve; service_role only,
                           re-checks the *mapped* user's role against the
                           console's own thresholds
  0015_certification       shareable certificates; anon certificate_verify
                           returns exactly four facts plus a verdict
  0016_public_status       per-site public status page, off by default,
                           counts and percentages only

Shared gate yf_can_read_site(text) and yf_is_service_role() are defined in
0009; 0011-0016 depend on them, and 0016 needs missions.completed_at from
0012, so these must be applied in filename order after 0007_rbac.sql.

e2e/fakerest.py gains a demo identity kind, the write triggers, two table
routes and 35 more RPC handlers (40 total) so the offline suites can cover
all of it. ops/tests/test_migrate.py gains five assertions for the OPT-IN
gate, the baseline set, banner placement inside the 400-byte scan window,
rollback blocks, and ordering after 0007.

docs/FEATURE-CONTRACTS.md (922 lines) is the authoritative spec every
downstream component codes against: exact table columns, RPC argument
names and types, return shapes, and the calling role for each.

Validated against a real PostgreSQL 16 instance, not only the fakes: all
16 migrations apply cleanly from empty, a 109-check behavioural suite
passes (demo isolation, cross-site write rejection, replay-as-of
correctness, share payload leak checks, inbound role gating, certificate
field allow-list, status-page leak checks, reaper scoping), every
rollback block runs in reverse, and re-application is idempotent.

Suites re-run individually after the change: core 8, ops 135, e2e 35,
sim/connector/detector/notifier/copilot all green. No regressions.

