From 5576911dfd74c05cf114f1e0cfd50bd3259b21a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 14:01:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] feat: finish the VDA 5050 conformance tester and the
 zero-signup sandbox
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two halves of the yantrika.ai acquisition funnel, completed from the
partial work committed in 0eaacaf.

CONFORMANCE TESTER (tools/conformance, 85 -> 188 tests)
The engine was sound but had never been observed failing: fake_robots.py
and harness.py existed and NO test imported either, so all 85 prior tests
were unit tests of spec/model and not one of the 52 checks had ever fired
in anger. Added test_checks.py, test_sim_integration.py, test_capture.py,
test_report.py and 26 isolated defect fixtures so every check has a case
that makes it fail on purpose. That exposed four real engine bugs, all
fixed:
  * protocol.topic_scheme was UNFALSIFIABLE — only the four known
    sub-topics were subscribed, so a wrong scheme could never be seen and
    the check always reported "conformant"
  * retained messages from the retain probe were re-fed as fresh evidence,
    failing one defect three times
  * connection.retained double-charged a vehicle publishing no connection
  * factsheet.published claimed "including after factsheetRequest" in
    --passive mode, where no such request is ever sent
New capture/replay path (capture.py + `yantra-conform replay`) so an
integrator can hand over a session file instead of broker access; replay
is stdlib-only and reproduces a live report check-for-check.

ZERO-SIGNUP SANDBOX (ops, 150 -> 177 tests)
Added ops/yantraops/sandbox_http.py — a stdlib HTTP door
(`yantraops sandbox-serve`) a static "Try it" button can hit: POST
/api/demo/session returns 201 JSON or a 303 straight into the console,
with per-IP rate limiting, two concurrency ceilings, and no caller-supplied
site_id or TTL anywhere. Plus systemd units for the door and the reaper.
Fixed a real quality bug: the driver's first tick teleported every robot up
to 28m from where the seeder parked it, orphaning the telemetry trail —
SandboxDriver.adopt_live_fleet() now continues from the live fleet.

Full suite green: ops 177, e2e 35, conformance 188, copilot 85, core 8,
sim/connector/notifier/detector all passing.

Known security gap found during this work and NOT yet fixed — see the next
commit: demo_sandbox_insert constrains commands.site_id but not
commands.robot_id, and the sim/connector approved-command pollers do not
filter by site.

