could insert a commands row naming a REAL robot with status already
'approved', bypassing the human approval gate. demo_sandbox_insert checked
only site_id; commands.robot_id is bare text with no same-site constraint;
INSERT was table-wide so status/decided_by/decided_at were attacker-chosen.
Downstream, sim's poll_commands had NO site filter and yantrabridge's had
one only when --site was passed, so a service-key executor would have
published a VDA 5050 instantAction to an attacker-supplied serial.
Fixed in three layers: tightened RLS (verified on real Postgres, idempotent,
and skips with a NOTICE on a project without 0009), mandatory site scoping
in both pollers, and closed e2e/fakerest.py's ON CONFLICT divergence.
The audit found the same class of gap on robot_telemetry and
maintenance_findings (both fixed) and on missions.robots (policy written
but shipped commented out — our own sandbox violates it today; root cause
and one-line fix recorded in the migration).
BREAKING: yantrabridge --commands now refuses to start without a site.
Chosen over defaulting, which would either execute the wrong thing or stop
silently. yantrasim is unaffected (its default already equals the site it
publishes into).

2) FUNNEL — the two finished features are now reachable and findable
nginx proxies /api/demo/ to the sandbox door with an http-context
limit_req_zone in front of the unauthenticated POST; both boot scripts now
install *.timer (the reaper would never have landed) and document the
service_role env file it needs; the landing page's primary CTA is a zero-JS
form with fetch enhancement; and marketing/vda-5050-conformance-test.html
exists at the filename every generated report hard-codes, with the 52-check
table rendered from the tool's own rule set. 286 internal links resolved
through the nginx layout, 0 dead. Also fixed: /docs/*.md had no mime type,
so every marketing->docs link downloaded a file instead of showing it.
aws/validate.sh was already failing 5 checks when this started — its
grep-based unit lint could not handle the oneshot reaper unit or backslash
continuations; the lint was fixed rather than the units.

3) SIMULATOR — two real VDA 5050 v2.1 violations, plus one they exposed
Stale orderUpdateIds were rejected silently; 6.5 requires an in-band
errors[] entry (orderUpdateError/WARNING) — the docstring asserting
otherwise was backwards. Superseded order actions vanished without a
terminal status, violating 6.9. Fixing the second exposed a latent bug:
build_state reported RUNNING under a self-generated actionId while the
terminal status used the order's id, so no order action ever reported
RUNNING under the id master control sent. Each fix verified by reverting it
and watching the tests fail.
Conformance score against a real broker: A 98.2 (1 fail) -> A 99.0 (0 fail).

